.TE
.SH Authentication
All channels except \f[CR]CHAN_CONTROL\f[R] require prior
authentication.
Unauthenticated requests on other channels receive an error response.
Authentication is performed by sending an \f[CR]auth\f[R] message on
\f[CR]CHAN_CONTROL\f[R] with a valid token.
.SH Session lifecycle
.IP "1." 3
Protocol version is set to \f[CR]PROTOCOL_V2\f[R].
.IP "2." 3
Frame read loop begins.
.IP "3." 3
Each frame is dispatched to the appropriate channel handler.
.IP "4." 3
On disconnect or error, \f[CR]debug_cleanup()\f[R] and
\f[CR]observe_cleanup()\f[R] are called.
